# Run 2026-10-31, boot A2: the A1 superflat world rebooted with (plan step A2)
#   toml [monster_box] vaultMode = false, [dandelion_maturing] richSoilTicks = 0
#   server.properties spawn-monsters=true, difficulty=normal
# Rows: config switches that need a restart, mob cap levels, whistle arrows, crop season growth fields.
pace 2

## SQ-A2-BOOT | reboot clean
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException).*(creativeengineering|creative_delight)
> pbot spawn qa 0 -60 0
> time set noon
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> pbot status
expect ceperfbot ok

## SQ-MB-07 | vaultMode off: box breaks after spawning (Quark behaviour)
> setblock 20 -60 -24 quark:monster_box
> tp qa 18 -60 -24
sleep 5
> execute if block 20 -60 -24 quark:monster_box
expect Test failed
> execute positioned 20 -60 -24 run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,distance=..24]

## SQ-DM-02 | richSoilTicks 0: a Rich Soil dandelion stays plain
> setblock -10 -61 14 farmersdelight:rich_soil
> setblock -10 -60 14 minecraft:dandelion
> tp qa -10 -60 11
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
sleep 60
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute if block -10 -60 14 minecraft:dandelion
expect Test passed

## SQ-MCL-02 | one player at night: level 0, about 289 chunks
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> time set 18000
sleep 90
> ceperf mobcap
look overworld about 289 spawnable chunks, level 0; monster count climbing toward vanilla 70

## SQ-MCL-03 | two players 600 apart: level 1, back to 0 together
> pbot spawn qb 600 -60 0
sleep 20
> ceperf mobcap
> tp qb 20 -60 0
sleep 30
> ceperf mobcap
look apart about 578 chunks and level 1; together back to level 0 once below 400
> pbot remove qb

## SQ-MCL-04 | forced level 2: hostiles settle near 25, none far out
# needs [perf] mobCapForceLevel = 2 set in the toml BEFORE the boot (a running server does not reload the toml);
# run on its own restart (A2: after a2_variants; B1: on the B1b boot), then set it back to -1
sleep 10
# a fresh boot spawns nothing near a just-joined bot for about 2.5 min (seen 10-31, level 0 too): wait it out
sleep 160
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> time set 18000
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
sleep 120
> ceperf mobcap
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:zombie]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:skeleton]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:spider]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:creeper]
> execute as @e[type=#zq:monsters,limit=1,sort=furthest] run data get entity @s Pos
look the four counts sum to about 25 (not 70); the farthest monster within about 90 blocks of 0 0 (perf.md 17); the toml switch is read live (if the level line still says auto, it is not)

## SQ-PF16-02 | whistling arrow still pulls animals
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
> time set noon
> summon minecraft:cow 6 -60 6
> summon minecraft:cow 7 -60 5
> summon minecraft:sheep 5 -60 7
> summon nock_enough_arrows:whistling_arrow 14 -60 14 {inGround:1b,pickup:0b}
sleep 15
> execute positioned 14 -60 14 if entity @e[type=#minecraft:animals_spawnable_on,distance=..4]
> execute positioned 14 -60 14 if entity @e[type=minecraft:cow,distance=..4]
> kill @e[type=nock_enough_arrows:whistling_arrow]
look cows and sheep walk to the arrow (second check passes); after the kill they stop following; a summoned arrow that never "joins" the tracker = the whistle needs a shot arrow (client CQ-PF16-02)
reject (?i)unknown entity

## SQ-CS-03 | winter: open field behind the glass-roofed field; spring: ahead
# measure = mean wheat age per field (`zq ages`), first line open field (x 100), second glass field (x 120);
# 2 min at randomTickSpeed 30 ripens almost nothing, so ripe counts were noise (10-31 first run)
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
> forceload add 96 -4 132 12
> fill 96 -61 -4 132 -61 12 minecraft:grass_block
> fill 100 -61 0 108 -61 8 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock 104 -61 4 minecraft:water
> fill 120 -61 0 128 -61 8 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock 124 -61 4 minecraft:water
> fill 119 -57 -1 129 -57 9 minecraft:glass
> tp qa 114 -60 -6
> fill 100 -60 0 108 -60 8 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> fill 120 -60 0 128 -60 8 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> setblock 104 -60 4 minecraft:air
> setblock 124 -60 4 minecraft:air
> season set MID_WINTER
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 30
sleep 120
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> zq ages 100 -60 0 108 -60 8 minecraft:wheat
> zq ages 120 -60 0 128 -60 8 minecraft:wheat
> fill 100 -60 0 108 -60 8 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> fill 120 -60 0 128 -60 8 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> setblock 104 -60 4 minecraft:air
> setblock 124 -60 4 minecraft:air
> season set MID_SPRING
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 30
sleep 120
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> zq ages 100 -60 0 108 -60 8 minecraft:wheat
> zq ages 120 -60 0 128 -60 8 minecraft:wheat
look winter: open mean below glass mean (about 3/4 of the growth); spring: open mean above glass mean (about 5/4)

